<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
   Auto Backup rules for API 30 and below (`android:fullBackupContent`).

   Backup is currently disabled outright — see `android:allowBackup="false"` and the reasoning above
   it in AndroidManifest.xml. These rules are therefore not consulted today. They exist so that the
   exclusion survives anyone turning backup back on: a captured log is other apps' logcat output and
   must not leave the device, and Auto Backup includes all of `getFilesDir()` by default.

   `logs/` is `SavedLogs.logsDir`, relative to `filesDir`. The two spellings have to agree.

   Not listed, because Auto Backup never includes them in the first place: `getCacheDir()`, which is
   where the live capture's temp file and the `log_shares/` zip staging live. If a future change moves
   either of those into `filesDir`, it needs a line here.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude
        domain="file"
        path="logs/" />
</full-backup-content>
